OK, first a very good place to start if you're not familiar with alpha=20
machines is the "www.alphalinux.org" It has heaps of info about the inter=
nals=20
of alpha, and a good article about the bootloader.
>
> Is there a rough outline of the install, up anywhere? or a good descrip=
tion
> of what should be done?

OK, I'll give an outline:
First the bootloader to use is srm.
when you have the srm prompt, you can use the command "show dev" to show =
what=20
devices is installed, if you have a cdrom it should come up as dkaxxx. Th=
en=20
you have your gentoo-alpha boot cdrom in the cdrom drive and enter "boot=20
dkaxxx" "enter". Then it should boot up much like the x86. You can use th=
e=20
installation documents for x86, but there are some differences.
When you use fdisk, make sure that the disk have a "bsd disklabel", if no=
t you=20
wouldn't be able to boot from it.
when you emerge the bootloader, do not use grub, but aboot.
post any problems that arise on this list when they show up, and we'll he=
lp=20
you.

I still remember my first go at installing on an alpha machine. Took me=20
forever to get it to boot because I forgot to make the bsd label.

hope this is helpfull.
- --=20
Sigurd Stordal
President of GOGS
Experimental Petrologist
