Use any other method of booting alpha into Linux. i.e. Debian CD.
Once you get that running, and network configured, you can get
stage tarball (only rc1 is available now, I think) and go from there.
I sudgest starting from stage 1, since emerge -up world will have
to update everything anyways.

Another thing is to specify "~alpha" in ACCEPT_HEYWORDS in make.conf
Because many packages are marked as unstabe on alpha. I also
had to modify many ebuilds to add "~alpha" to KEYWORDS, so that emerge noti=
ces
them.

	Ilya.

