>
> You can follow the x86 instructions pretty closely.  There is no 
> liveCD except for rc_1, but it works fine.  Just make sure you know 
> what type of processor it is when you modify your CFLAGS in 
> /etc/make.conf
>
> Some caveats: ---On your boot drive, make sure you leave the first two 
> cylinders unpartitioned.  You must use a BSD disklabel if booting from 
> SRM. Start your /boot partition at cylinder #3.
>
> ---Be sure you have the line with "ACCEPT_KEYWORDS=~alpha" uncommented 
> out of /etc/make.conf before you start stage2.
>
> ---The kernel sources to emerge are "emerge alpha-sources"
>
> ---In your kernel config, make sure to select "SRM as a bootloader" if 
> booting from SRM (This is _required_ if you do not use the "generic" 
